# Modelfile for the mdsplit workload.
#
#   ollama create mdsplit-qwen -f docs/Modelfile.mdsplit
#   mcp-md-splitter -translate -dir chunks/ -lang de -llm-model mdsplit-qwen
#
# This workload is not a chat. It is a few hundred short, isolated requests
# with no history, and a server tuned for long conversations pays for context
# it never uses on every one of them.

FROM qwen3.5:35b

# --- Context -------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Ollama defaults this model to a very large slot - 128000 in one measured
# case. A slot that size allocates KV cache and checkpoints per request; the
# log showed 32 checkpoints of 62.8 MiB for a 115-token prompt. Nothing here
# needs it.
#
# The arithmetic: in block mode the largest request is the batched list of
# short fragments, roughly 250 tokens of rules plus 400 of fragments plus up
# to 300 of glossary, answered in kind - call it 2000. In chunk mode a part of
# `-size N` characters is about N/3 tokens in and the same again out, so
# -size 8000 needs ~6000. 8192 covers both with room; drop to 4096 if you only
# ever run block mode.
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192

# --- Determinism ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# Translation is not a creative task, and a rerun of one rejected part should
# produce the same answer as the run that rejected it.
PARAMETER temperature 0
PARAMETER top_k 1

# --- The one that matters ------------------------------------------------
#
# Ollama's default repeat_penalty of 1.1 is wrong for this. Technical prose
# repeats on purpose: a table where two cells both read "one", a glossary term
# used in four fragments, the ⟦0⟧ markers that must come back exactly as sent.
# Penalising repetition pushes the model to vary precisely what has to stay
# identical - and a changed marker means the whole reply is discarded.
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.0

# --- What does NOT belong here -------------------------------------------
#
# Two settings that look right and are not:
#
#   PARAMETER think false
#     `ollama create` accepts it and reports success. It has no effect: the
#     model still produced 4716 output tokens for a one-sentence translation,
#     identical to the base. Thinking is a request field, not a model
#     parameter - pass -llm-reasoning none instead.
#
#   PARAMETER stop "<think>" "</think>"
#     Worse than useless. A reasoning model writes its reasoning first, so the
#     stop fires just before the answer: 4691 tokens generated, full cost paid,
#     and the reply comes back empty with finish_reason "stop" - the very
#     signal a client reads as "complete".
#
# --- No SYSTEM here, on purpose ------------------------------------------
#
# Ollama uses a Modelfile SYSTEM only when the request carries no system
# message, and mdsplit sends one: the translation rules, the placeholder
# convention, and the glossary entries that apply to this fragment. A SYSTEM
# line here would be silently ignored in normal use.
#
# It takes effect only when the client suppresses its own system message,
# which -llm-user-template does. See Modelfile.mdsplit-de for that variant.
